島ごと全部失くしたってこと？
You lost the whole island?!

359
00:34:42,078 --> 00:34:48,018
What? No! What I'm saying is I knew where it was the whole time! I...

360
00:34:48,108 --> 00:34:54,738
What'd she see in you? A beautiful young woman like her, with an old hag like you?

361
00:34:55,428 --> 00:34:59,318
What?! I'm young, beautiful!

362
00:34:59,408 --> 00:35:02,138
Yeah, and I'm the goddess of death...

363
00:35:02,138 --> 00:35:06,138
じゃあ私は死神でも名乗ろうかしら。
Look at you, you're creeping slowly towards your grave...

364
00:35:06,138 --> 00:35:07,038
はぁ!?
Ha?!

365
00:35:07,138 --> 00:35:12,138
セクシー船長なんですが!?
I'm a sexy captain! Pirate captain!

366
00:35:13,138 --> 00:35:14,638
まあいいでしょう。
Yes. Well...

367
00:35:15,138 --> 00:35:19,638
ここへあなたを呼ぶのは復讐のため。
Moving on... I've brought you here to exact my revenge on you, captain,

368
00:35:19,638 --> 00:35:22,638
あなたの恋人は……
for the untimely death of your lover.

369
00:35:23,138 --> 00:35:28,638
あなたにその命を奪われた!
I know that you were the one to take her life and I will not stand for it! You will suffer by my hands!

370
00:35:29,138 --> 00:35:31,638
はぁぁ!?
Ha?!

371
00:35:32,638 --> 00:35:38,638
実は……このクエストはただの邪魔。
You know, this quest was just a distraction. It was meant to keep you from watching over your...

372
00:35:38,638 --> 00:35:41,638
あなたが目を離してしまうようにね。
beautiful, and sexy lover,

373
00:35:42,638 --> 00:35:46,638
そして私があなたの代わりになる。
and leave room for me to take your place.

374
00:35:46,638 --> 00:35:51,138
でも彼女はこの世を去り、私の心には穴があいた。
But now your lover is dead, and I am left with a hole in my heart.

375
00:35:51,638 --> 00:35:54,638
あなたにはここで報いを受けてもらいましょう。
You will pay for what you've done here and now!

376
00:35:54,638 --> 00:35:57,138
そこまでだ!
That's enough of that!

377
00:35:58,138 --> 00:36:02,638
死神!? なぜここに……深夜は忙しいんじゃないだって?
Death?! What are you doing here? Don't you usually work the graveyard shift?

378
00:36:03,138 --> 00:36:12,138
私の愛しい人を生き返らせてくれるわけでもないなら回れ右してさっさと仕事に戻るがいいわ。
Unless you're planning on bringing back my beautiful little bird to me, you can turn right around and poof yourself back to wherever it is you came from!

379
00:36:13,138 --> 00:36:19,638
お前は私を知ったつもりになっているだけだぜ。そこにいる「船長」のこともな。
Well, maybe you don't know me as well as you pretend to, or the pirate captain as well as you think either.

380
00:36:20,138 --> 00:36:27,138
止めはしない。その人間を罰したいなら好きにしろ。私はない……行く……
Look, you can go ahead and smite that human if you like. I'm not going to try and stop you, but I really think you might regret doing that.

381
00:36:30,638 --> 00:36:38,138
恋人を手にかえた人間の肩を持つつもり!? 見損なったわ!
You would take the side of someone so cruel that they would take the life of their own lover?! I expected better of you!

382
00:36:39,138 --> 00:36:47,138
っていうか彼女がこの世にいない今、私が彼女を嫁にするのも無理では……?
Besides, how am I supposed to take their place and make that beautiful cream puff my wife if this fool here has killed her?

383
00:36:48,138 --> 00:36:51,138
えっ待って! 船長を嫁に!?
Wait! What? You want the captain?!

384
00:36:51,638 --> 00:36:59,138
いや? 何が船長よ……。あなたのようなババアを誰が嫁にしたいっていうの?
No, where did you even get that from? Why would you even think that I would want someone as old and badly dressed as you?

385
00:36:59,638 --> 00:37:06,638
でもでも……私が欲しいのはあの「宝箱」だけ! ツインテールで美少女無罪なあいの人だけなの!
No, it has always been that treasure box of wonder, that twin-tail talent, that sweet girl who can do no sin that you kept back on land,

386
00:37:07,138 --> 00:37:17,138
彼女が欲しいの! あなたは論外。
that is the one I have wanted! You? No, not at all.

387
00:37:18,138 --> 00:37:22,138
その「宝箱」本人をババア呼ばわりしたのは誰かな?
Yeah, but you just called that treasure box of wonder a hag not two minutes ago!

388
00:37:23,138 --> 00:37:29,138
いったい何を言ってるの!? 彼女じゃなくてこいつをババアと呼んだの! ノットマイ美しいブライトトビー
What are you even talking about? I call this wrinkly old wreck here in front of me a hag, not my beautiful bride-to-be!

389
00:37:30,138 --> 00:37:36,138
傑作だ。まだ分からないのか? 何がおかしい!
Oh man, this is rich. You really have no idea, do you, Nerissa? Why are you laughing?

390
00:37:37,138 --> 00:37:41,138
17歳なんですが!
I'm not old! I'm 17!

391
00:37:42,138 --> 00:37:54,138
見せてやろう、ピゲに隠れていた正体をな! ピゲの船長は仮の姿!
Let me see if I can help you here. Maybe all the beauty is being hidden by a... Let's see... I'm not the pirate captain!

392
00:37:54,638 --> 00:38:03,638
そう、この女性こそヒゲの船長の恋人。お前が恋し、亡くしたと思い込んでいたマリンその人だ!
No, she is actually his much more beautiful lover, who you claimed to love. That's right, here is the Marine you thought was lost!

393
00:38:04,138 --> 00:38:08,638
ありえない! 私が気づかないはずが……!
That's not possible! I would have known, or I never would have...

394
00:38:09,138 --> 00:38:14,638
言いいたいことは色々あるが、なぜ気づかなかった?
I have a lot to say, but my most pressing question is, how on earth did you not know?

395
00:38:15,138 --> 00:38:25,138
だって見た目全然違うじゃん! ヒゲ付けただけであんなに醜くなるなんて!
You know, that's fair because they look nothing alike, but how am I supposed to know? How did such a simple mustache make her look so decidedly unattractive?

396
00:38:25,638 --> 00:38:28,638
ただの付けヒゲでしょうが! 付いてても可愛いだろうが!
It's just a mustache! I was still cute!

397
00:38:29,138 --> 00:38:34,138
もちろんですよ。あいつがバカなんです。
Of course you are, dear. She's just an imbecile. Wait, why am I so mean? Let me change that.

398
00:38:35,138 --> 00:38:45,138
だがあのバカでは、死神との契約を破ったあなたを守れない。あなたとの魂を頂かなくては。
Anyway, but my dear, her stupidity can't protect you now that you've broken our deal. A broken deal with Death means that your soul is mine.

399
00:38:46,138 --> 00:38:57,138
梅やめ愚か者! 付サヒゲごとき見破れずに愛だの恋だの! お前のせいで彼女は魂を奪われるのだ!
This is all your fault, Drama Queen! You claimed to love Marine, but you had no idea that she was hiding behind a mustache! Because of your idiocy... her soul is mine now!

400
00:38:58,138 --> 00:39:04,138
私のせい!? そんなバカな! そもそも彼女はここに現れるはずじゃなかった!
Me?! How am I supposed to know? She was never supposed to be on this quest in the first place!

401
00:39:05,138 --> 00:39:12,138
待て、もし彼女が生きているなら、逆にヒゲの船長はあの世に……。あの世は死神の領域!
Wait, if she's here, then that must mean the real pirate captain is dead. And that's your domain, Ms. Reaper!

402
00:39:12,638 --> 00:39:20,138
こうなる前に止めることもできたはず! お前のせいだ死神! 無罪! 無罪!
If the captain is gone, it means you have had some responsibility in all of this. You could have stopped all of this at any time!

403
00:39:21,138 --> 00:39:29,638
私のせいだと!? 私がヒゲの船長をやったわけじゃない。私はマリンに頼まれて、正体を隠す手伝いをしてやっただけだぜ。
Oh, so you want to blame me for all of this? It wasn't me who killed the captain. I only protected Marine after she begged for me to help hide her identity from you!

404
00:39:30,138 --> 00:39:34,638
彼女は亡き恋人のためにこのバカげた冒険を終わらせたかったのだす!
She just wanted to complete your stupid quest in honor of her... lover.

405
00:39:35,138 --> 00:39:42,638
死神が変装を手伝う義理はないでしょう! お前が隠したりしなければ、こんな回りくどいことをせず愛を伝えられたのに!
Yes, but you shouldn't have agreed to hide her! I would have known if you hadn't meddled and I would have given her my favor without this quest!

406
00:39:43,138 --> 00:39:45,138
魂……?
My soul...?

407
00:39:46,138 --> 00:39:48,138
彼女の前で手荒な真実はしたくないわ。
You're lucky she's here to keep me from hurting you.

408
00:39:48,638 --> 00:39:52,638
来いよ。お門違いだがな。あの……この間は……
I'd like to see you try. Besides, this one wasn't me.

409
00:39:53,138 --> 00:39:58,638
マリンが……お茶にバナナを入れたんです。
Um... Marine... put bananas in the tea.

410
00:39:59,138 --> 00:40:03,138
え!? でも…… weren't the captain... 重度のバナナアレルギー……
Wait, but wasn't the captain severely allergic to bananas?

411
00:40:02,722 --> 00:40:07,302
重度のバナナアレルギー……そういうことだったのか……。
Severe banana allergy... So that's how it was...

412
00:40:08,482 --> 00:40:15,502
マリンも冒険したいのにダメって言われたから、お茶にバナナを……。
Marine wanted to go on an adventure too, but she was told no, so she put bananas in the tea...

413
00:40:16,662 --> 00:40:19,542
そんな……予想外だ。
No way... That's unexpected.

414
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:27,282
人の生死に干渉したあなたは本来許されないが、しかし、取り逃した魂を追う私をあなたが手伝ってくれたあの夜から
Meddling in matters of life and death is normally unforgivable, but ever since that night when you helped me chase after an escaped soul—

415
00:40:28,282 --> 00:40:31,782
あなたを想わずにはいられない。
I haven't been able to stop thinking about you.

416
00:40:32,142 --> 00:40:37,322
死神の心まで奪うとはね……ずいぶん幸運な女性だ。
To steal the heart of the Grim Reaper... consider yourself a lucky woman.

417
00:40:38,162 --> 00:40:40,442
あ、あの夜って！？ナイト！ドン！ドン！
Wh-What night?! Don't you dare!

418
00:40:40,442 --> 00:40:48,502
罪を犯した彼女でも私は守りたい。彼女が恋人の命を奪った事実は隠し通す。悲しい事故だったんだ。
I want to protect this woman from her own crimes even in death. No one else has to know that she was the one who took the life of her lover. It can all just be an unfortunate accident.

419
00:40:49,542 --> 00:40:53,002
バナナの皮は滑りやすいし仕方ない。
Banana peels are known to be slippery, so it can't be helped.

420
00:40:53,262 --> 00:40:55,042
カリオペ！！させない！
Calliope!! I won't let you!

421
00:40:55,042 --> 00:40:59,762
死神に連れ去られたらもう終わりなのよ！
She'll never be able to escape the Reaper's clutches, and I can't allow that to happen!

422
00:41:00,002 --> 00:41:05,402
そもそもカリオペ、全てはあなたのせいでしょう！
After all, this is your fault, Mori, for even letting her take this deal in the first place!

423
00:41:05,902 --> 00:41:09,642
でもバナナは……死神のせいにすればいい。
But the banana... Just blame it on the Reaper.

424
00:41:10,702 --> 00:41:17,702
来てマリン……私ならあなたを死から守れる。天の世界なら死神の手は届かない。
Come, Marine... I can protect you from even death itself. She can't get you in the realm of the immortals.

425
00:41:18,022 --> 00:41:19,462
貴様っ！でも……。
You bastard! But...

426
00:41:19,782 --> 00:41:25,862
黙って。あなたをかばった女神として名が残る！
Shut up. You'll be known as the goddess who protected the banana bandit!

427
00:41:26,242 --> 00:41:27,862
神々の恥さらしだな。
The other gods won't be very happy with you.

428
00:41:28,322 --> 00:41:30,162
それがどうしたの？なぜ？
And you think that matters to me? Why?

429
00:41:30,422 --> 00:41:34,062
バナナ……？だれがそれを……。
Banana...?! Don't blame it on her, of course!

430
00:41:34,342 --> 00:41:39,202
いや……マリンは私が連れていく！無駄話は終わりだネリッサ！
No... Marine, I'm taking you! Enough talk, take this, Nerissa!

431
00:41:39,582 --> 00:41:44,702
無罪～！！待て！待て！待て！
Not guilty~!! Wait! Wait! Wait!

432
00:41:48,382 --> 00:41:55,802
お疲れ様。ありがとう。ありがとう。ありがとう。
Good work. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

433
00:41:56,242 --> 00:42:03,482
そして、いいニュースガールズ、ミュージックチームはすでにいるから、私たちもあそこへ行ってスーパー歌ってみたのパフォーマンスを見せよう！
And good news, girls, it seems like the music team is already ready for us, so why don't we head over and show them our super cool song performance!

434
00:42:04,153 --> 00:42:12,153
行こう！やっほー！
Let's go! Yay!

435
00:42:24,189 --> 00:42:31,153
荒れ狂う季節の中を 二人は一人きり さらり 明け行く夕日の中を 今夜も昼下がり さらり
Through the raging seasons, just the two of us, smoothly. Through the dawning sunset, even this afternoon, smoothly

436
00:42:32,653 --> 00:42:39,623
どれほど朽ち果てようと 最後にゃ笑いたい 何のために 戦おうとも動機は愛がいい
No matter how much we may decay, in the end I want to smile. Whatever we fight for, our motive should be love

437
00:42:40,983 --> 00:42:46,843
あれほど生きてきたけど 全ては夢みたい あれもこれも 魅力的でも私は君がいい
No matter how much I've lived, it all feels like a dream. This and that may be charming, but I want you

438
00:42:52,183 --> 00:42:54,383
新しい日々は 探さずとも常に ここに
New days, without even searching, are always right here

439
00:42:57,153 --> 00:43:02,653
新しい日々は 探さずとも常に ここに
New days, without even searching, are always right here

440
00:43:04,153 --> 00:43:12,153
色々見てきたけれど この瞳は永遠に きらり
I've seen all sorts of things, but these eyes sparkle forever

441
00:43:13,353 --> 00:43:21,153
あれほど生きてきたけど 全ては夢みたい あれもこれも 魅力的でも私は君がいい
No matter how much I've lived, it all feels like a dream. This and that may be charming, but I want you

442
00:43:22,653 --> 00:43:27,653
魅力的でも 私は君がいい
Even if it's charming, I want you

443
00:43:29,153 --> 00:43:41,153
どこにいたの 探してたよ 連れてって 連れてって 何もかも 捨ててくよ
Where were you? I was searching for you. Take me with you, take me with you. I'll throw everything away

444
00:43:42,153 --> 00:43:53,153
どこまでも どこまでも 荒れ狂う 季節の中も 群衆の中も 君とならば さらり さらり
To the ends of the earth, through the raging seasons and the crowds, if it's with you, smoothly, smoothly

445
00:43:54,153 --> 00:44:04,153
新しい日々も 拙い過去も 全てがきらり
New days and awkward pasts, everything sparkles

446
00:44:21,153 --> 00:44:28,153
無くしてしまったものを 振り返って ほろり 時には途方に暮れて ただ風に吹かれて ゆらり
Looking back at what I've lost and shedding a tear, sometimes feeling lost and just swaying in the wind

447
00:44:37,153 --> 00:44:44,153
息せき切ってきたの 行き先は決めたの 迷わずに行きたいけど保証はしないよ
Breathless I came, I've decided where I'm going. I want to go without hesitation, but I can't guarantee anything

448
00:44:45,153 --> 00:44:53,153
何か分かったようで 何も分かってなくて だけどそれが分かって本当に良かった
It feels like I understood something yet didn't understand anything at all, but realizing that was truly for the best

449
00:44:54,153 --> 00:45:02,168
新しい日々は 探さずとも常に ここに 常にここに ここに
New days, without even searching, are always right here, always right here, right here

450
00:45:02,168 --> 00:45:05,968
色々見てきたけれど この瞳は永遠に きらり
I've seen various things, but these eyes are forever shimmering.

451
00:45:10,668 --> 00:45:15,668
あれほど生きてきたけど 全ては夢みたい
I've lived so much, but it's all like a dream.

452
00:45:16,668 --> 00:45:24,568
あれもこれも 魅力的でも 私は君がいい
No matter how attractive this or that is, I want you.

453
00:45:33,168 --> 00:45:36,668
どこにいたの 探してたよ
Where were you? I was searching for you.

454
00:45:37,168 --> 00:45:44,468
連れてって 連れてって 何もかも 捨ててくよ
Take me away, take me away, I'll throw everything away.

455
00:45:45,168 --> 00:45:53,668
どこまでも どこまでも 荒れ狂う 季節の中も 群衆の中も
No matter how far, no matter how far... Even in the raging seasons, even in the crowd...

456
00:45:54,168 --> 00:45:59,668
君とならば さらり さらり 新しい日々も
If I'm with you, effortlessly, effortlessly... The new days too...

457
00:45:59,968 --> 00:46:06,668
拙い過去も 全てがきらり
...and my clumsy past, everything shines brightly.

458
00:46:16,668 --> 00:46:21,668
Thank you guys so much! Thank you!

459
00:46:22,168 --> 00:46:26,168
Thank you!

460
00:46:28,668 --> 00:46:32,168
Bye-bye! See you later!

461
00:46:33,168 --> 00:46:36,668
Thank you for coming, too!

462
00:46:36,668 --> 00:46:42,168
Yeah, no problem. Happy to be here. Congrats on 3D!

463
00:46:42,168 --> 00:46:47,168
Thank you! Made it so special to have you two as guests...
Thank you! It made it so special to have you two as guests...

464
00:46:47,168 --> 00:46:52,168
...and to get to sing with you too, that's crazy!

465
00:46:52,168 --> 00:46:57,168
So we're going to say goodbye for a few seconds and I'll be right back. Let's go!

466
00:46:57,368 --> 00:46:59,668
Bye-bye!

467
00:47:17,168 --> 00:47:26,168
So this last song for today is actually going to be the titular track of my new EP, In My Feelings.

468
00:47:26,168 --> 00:47:35,168
I really worked hard on this song. I think it came out great, so I hope you guys will enjoy listening to my first live performance of it.

469
00:47:36,168 --> 00:47:38,668
それでは聴いてください。
So please listen.

